[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one issue, one fix queued. Its own cause table
says otherwise. Rendered, it shows more than one cause, and a footnote for reports that are
not a month flip at all.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is not one issue. Each problem in it now has a ticket of its own, with the reports it
covers.
</Callout>

## What the desk's own table shows

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## The problems, one ticket each

- **The shared parser reads day-first dates month first:
  [issue #1](https://github.com/frinux/mega-s01e03-support-kb/issues/1).** The `parser` row
  above, counted as the desk counts it: the reports footnoted under it stay there, where they
  are filed, and also have the one-day ticket. Every tenant on file writes
  the day first; the parser reads the month first, so day and month swap: "Our 7 April
  reminder went out on 4 July."
- **The `booking-v3` form hints `MM/DD/YYYY`, then reads the date day first:
  [issue #2](https://github.com/frinux/mega-s01e03-support-kb/issues/2).** The `hint` row
  above. The table marks it "no ticket of its own"; it has one now. People type what the hint
  tells them, month first, and the form reads it the tenant's way. Fixing the parser does not
  change the hint.
- **Bookings move by one day, not by a month:
  [issue #3](https://github.com/frinux/mega-s01e03-support-kb/issues/3).** The reports in the
  footnote under the table. "Tuesday 6 October showed as Monday." A parser that reads the month
  first swaps day and month; it cannot move a date by one day. Most likely a time-zone
  conversion: one report has the same meeting on Tuesday in Lisbon and on Monday in Toronto.

## How a report is placed

By the desk's own rules, the ones the table above runs (`causes.ts`), plus the desk's own
notes (`desk-notes.json`):

- the tenant decides the cause, not the reporter's browser. Intake's tag is a guess made from
  the browser locale; the "tagged as" column shows how often it guessed the other cause;
- a report from a tenant on `booking-v3` that came in through the form is `hint`; every other
  report from a day-first tenant is `parser`;
- a report the desk read as a one-day move stays counted where it is filed, and is footnoted
  there. It is not a month flip, so it also has the one-day ticket.

## Why they were merged

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges reports whose subject lines
match. All of these problems arrive under the same subjects: "Wrong day on the invite" and
"Month and day swapped?" each carry reports of every problem above. Matching on the subject
cannot keep them apart. The explorer on [triage](/kb/triage/dedupe) shows the same thing:
the same subject is not the same cause.

## What changes for the desk

- Ship the parser fix against its own ticket. The `hint` and one-day tickets stay open after
  it ships.
- Send new reports from a `booking-v3` form, and reports of a one-day move, to their own
  tickets, not to #4471.
- Decision 0001 needs a successor record that places reports by tenant, form and channel,
  not by subject. That is a new record, signed by its deciders; 0001 stays as it is.

